{#- Follows infloww.com/infloww-affiliate. -#}
<h2>The commission</h2>
<p>
  Earn 100% of their first year's subscription. Their first year's subscription is $0.
  There is no sign-up, referral link or payout threshold.
</p>

<h2>Theirs, for comparison</h2>
<p>
  Infloww's affiliate page offers to "earn 10% of their first year's subscription", and its terms (section 18) pay 20%
  of first-year fees for referring a Creator (infloww.com/infloww-affiliate and infloww.com/tos, pages stamped
  Oct 10, 2026).
</p>

<h2>The sincere version</h2>
<p>If Inflowwww saved you a bill, these help more than a commission would:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Star the repo</strong> on <a href="{{ site.repo }}">GitHub</a>, so the next agency finds it.</li>
  <li><strong>Send a fix.</strong> Some screens are NotBuiltYet; the <a href="{{ '/roadmap/' | url }}">roadmap</a> lists them. Open a <a href="{{ site.repo }}/pulls">pull request</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Report a bug</strong> with the steps to reproduce it, in the <a href="{{ site.repo }}/issues">issue tracker</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Write a post</strong> about how you run it: your VPS, your setup, what broke. Link the repo.</li>
</ul>
